# Architecture

Engineering constitution for full-stack products: **React + Vite** SPA, **Node** API, **Supabase** (Auth + Postgres). Proven layered design — no microservices, no GraphQL, no custom frameworks unless explicitly approved.

## Monorepo layout (new projects)

```
<repo>/
├── apps/
│   ├── web/                 # Vite React SPA (deployable)
│   └── api/                 # Node API (deployable)
├── packages/
│   └── shared/              # Zod schemas, types, constants — zero app imports
├── supabase/
│   └── migrations/          # sole source of DB truth
├── scripts/                 # dev orchestration, smoke tests
├── .github/workflows/       # CI
├── package.json             # npm workspaces root
├── .env.example
└── README.md
```

**Legacy layout** (`frontend/` + `backend/` at repo root) is acceptable during migration. New work follows `apps/*` when restructuring; do not mix both layouts in the same repo long term.

## System boundaries

```text
Browser
  ├─ Supabase Auth SDK     → login, session, token refresh only
  └─ HTTPS + Bearer JWT    → all business reads/writes

API (service_role)         → Postgres, RPC, R2
Postgres (app schema)      → system of record
R2 (optional)              → binary assets; keys in DB, never public URLs without proxy
```

**Hard rules**

- Frontend **never** uses service_role or reads business tables via anon key.
- Frontend **never** sets prices on write — server resolves from catalog.
- One catalog source of truth in Postgres (not static TS arrays in production).
- Schema changes only via `supabase/migrations/` — never “just run SQL in dashboard” without committing migration file.

## Layer model (API)

```text
routes/        HTTP adapter — parse, status codes, call service
services/      use-cases — orchestration, no raw SQL in routes
repositories/  Supabase SDK, PostgREST RPC, R2 — no business rules
plugins/       auth, CORS, request-id, error shape, rate limit
```

Routes stay thin. Services are unit-tested. Repositories are swappable.

## Layer model (web)

```text
app/           shell — routes, providers, query client
features/      domain UI — auth, shop, pos (co-located hooks + api)
components/    shared presentational — no domain logic
lib/           api-client, theme, formatters — no feature rules
```

Features expose a **public** `index.ts`. Other code imports `@/features/<name>`, never deep paths into feature internals.

## Dependency rules

| From | May import | Must NOT import |
|------|------------|-----------------|
| `packages/shared` | zod | any `apps/*` |
| `apps/api/routes` | services, shared, plugins | repositories |
| `apps/api/services` | repositories, shared | HTTP request/response types |
| `apps/api/repositories` | shared, DB clients | services, routes |
| `apps/web/features/*` | components, lib, shared, feature public APIs | `apps/api`, service_role |
| `apps/web/components` | lib, shared | feature internals |

Enforce with ESLint `import/no-restricted-paths` or `eslint-plugin-boundaries` when project grows.

## Deploy model

- **Two Vercel projects**: `apps/web` and `apps/api` (separate roots).
- **Three environments**: local, staging, production — separate Supabase projects for staging/prod.
- Build-time env (`VITE_*`) on web; runtime env on API.
- One `vercel.json` per app — no conflicting rewrites (no maintenance mode in app deploy config).

## State ownership

| Concern | Owner |
|---------|--------|
| Session / JWT | Supabase Auth (client) |
| Role / permissions | API `GET /api/me` — not direct PostgREST from browser |
| Server data | TanStack Query + API |
| UI ephemeral | `useState` |
| Multi-step local UI (cart lines) | `useReducer` in feature hook |

No Redux/Zustand unless three or more global client stores appear.

## What we deliberately skip

Microservices, GraphQL, event sourcing, Kubernetes for SMB apps, SSR/Next unless SEO blockers proven, BFF per client, CQRS packages for &lt;5 domains.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ Business data fetched with anon key from browser
- ❌ Client-sent `unitPrice` trusted on write
- ❌ Multiple SQL schema files contradicting runtime (`public` vs `anthea` vs ad-hoc)
- ❌ Logic in route handlers that belongs in services
- ❌ Feature A importing Feature B's components directly (use shared or public API)
